  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-06-16T13:10:56.916Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Ok so after installing, uninstalling, and reinstalling, several versions of visual studio and several versions of unity, i have managed to accomplish thus far:\n\ni was able to open the sample avatar project in unity 2019.xxx.x using the creator companion app. i was able to find the VRChat SDK option in the menu ribbon, and subsequently was able to export the sample package. I was very excited that I was able to transfer this exported package to my VRChat installation, and i could play as the sample avatar in game!!! woohoo!\n\nnow i have spent a lot of time trying to get my custom unity project to work within the creator companion. it turns out that no matter how i try to manipulate files and change version references, my custom unity project only works with Unity 2023. Now i understand that the creator companion only supports unity 2019.xx.x \n\nwell my project requires this more recent version of unity in order to function properly. i cant export a vrchat avatar package because the vrchat sdk menu strip item does not show up in my newer version of unity!! \n\nwhen can we expect the creator companion to support the most recent version of unity? surely by now VRChat SDK development has advanced beyond the year 2019. \n\nNo matter where i look for help, i cant seem to find anything or anyone who has the same problem i have. ive already submitted a bug report to unity3d and their engineering team. when will VRChat Creator companion support the latest version of unity? its time to move forward!!!",
